{"id": "EUVD-2026-93178", "enisaUuid": "63a473b0-bdd6-362a-9e4e-bcb4f4731c86", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: fix handling of NFSEXP_PNFS in the netlink codepath\n\nThe rework of how block layouts were checked moved the check for\nNFSEXP_PNFS out of nfsd4_setup_layout_type() and into the callers. That\npatch didn't account for the new call in nfsd4_setup_layout_type().", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30335038d4e25cf017abb0562f4f4eace4f58f96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f76017a7663c4ce5e379f8a8d39f032bdb1fd865"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vc4w-f249-26qv", "CVE-2026-98250"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "196d8115-4546-38f4-882d-c699b8c8f6af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da9baa5470dcb077a7c9806f0925c60b530c470b <30335038d4e25cf017abb0562f4f4eace4f58f96"}, {"id": "3981f356-2091-33dd-9c67-03c3198a74e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da9baa5470dcb077a7c9806f0925c60b530c470b <f76017a7663c4ce5e379f8a8d39f032bdb1fd865"}, {"id": "3affaf5f-c370-3a50-8b8b-3062225ebcaa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "69e9f0ee-1571-3f49-884a-033bbcc92261", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "af524bbc-581e-3046-badf-b832adddac27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d3a1f7a9-a932-3f50-8d5b-801a1b35e6bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d4e22420-7fa8-378a-bc8c-1ece890a97e8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}